  sheld  every sheld helps to prevent  helps to prevent covet 19 in  immunocompromised people for whom  vaccination does not provide adequate  protection to be clear heavy shelled is  not a treatment for coping 19 it's given  before exposure to help prevent  infection in someone who is just unable  to amount a full immune response to  vaccine  alberta's clinical experts have reviewed  the evidence for this product and have  provided a recommendation for its use in  albertans who may benefited from it the  most  starting tomorrow every shell will be  available to eligible albertans who have  solid organ or cell transplants or blood  cancer or are being treated with  specific immuno-compromising drugs  details regarding who is eligible to  receive have you shelled are available  at www.ahs  dot ca backslash covent  opt  as this is a very specific group access  to evasheld at this time will be  provided through specialist physicians  who treat these patients  please contact your specialist if you  believe every shell may be an option for  you  it is important to remember that new  research is happening all the time and  will continue to update albertans on  other advances to help protect them from  coven 19.  few measures in public health can  compare with the impact vaccines have  had over the years to reduce disease  disability and death from a variety of  infectious diseases this includes the  effectiveness of our cova 19 vaccine  program as i said many times the initial  cova 19 vaccine series as well as  are still  the most effective prevention tools that  we have they're the they're the best way  to prevent severe illness and death and  reduce the need for hospitalization so  please call today to make an appointment  or visit a location with vaccines  available on a walk-in basis in our  province  i'll close there and just add a note on  process  we'll continue to provide updated data  every week but we'll be moving these  in-person updates to every second week  